<!-- AT A GLANCE -->
<tr><td bgcolor="#fffdf9" style="background-color:#fffdf9;padding:16px 30px 0 30px;">
  <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td bgcolor="#b8860b" style="background-color:#b8860b;font-family:'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;color:#ffffff;padding:8px 14px;"><font color="#ffffff">AT A GLANCE</font></td></tr></table>
  <p style="font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#17313b;margin:12px 0 0 0;">
    Outside Lands packed up on Sunday and the city exhaled &#8212; which makes this the good part of a San Francisco August. The crowds thin, the fog thickens, and the free stuff comes out. <b>Stern Grove closes its 89th season this weekend</b> with Public Enemy on Saturday and Al Green on Sunday, and then that's it until next June. Around it: the Perseids peak Wednesday night, the 49ers open the preseason at Levi's on Thursday, and the Giants play seven home games in the next week alone. Late August belongs to the neighborhoods &#8212; Oakland Chinatown and Palo Alto both throw street festivals on the 22nd&#8211;23rd, the Castro blocks off Market on the 29th &#8212; and Labor Day weekend hands you Millbrae's art-and-wine sprawl plus a kite festival at Candlestick. Six of the picks below are free. Two are only-in-the-Bay (marked &#9733;).
  </p>
  <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin-top:12px;"><tr><td bgcolor="#fdf7e8" style="background-color:#fdf7e8;border-left:4px solid #b8860b;padding:10px 12px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#17313b;">
    <b style="font-family:'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#8a6508;">WEEKEND WEATHER &#8212; SAN FRANCISCO</b><br>
    <b>Fri Aug 14:</b> mostly sunny, high 69&#176;F &middot; <b>Sat Aug 15:</b> mostly sunny, high 68&#176;F &middot; <b>Sun Aug 16:</b> mostly sunny, high 67&#176;F. Nights mostly cloudy, lows around 55&#176;F, with a southwesterly breeze gusting into the low 20s mph. <b>No rain in the forecast</b> &#8212; the contingency this month is cold, not wet. Stern Grove sits in a shaded eucalyptus bowl that runs 8&#8211;10&#176;F below the rest of the city: bring a real jacket, a blanket, and long pants, not a picnic fantasy. Same advice for Candlestick Point on Sep 6, where the wind is the whole point.
  </td></tr></table>
  <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin-top:10px;"><tr><td bgcolor="#fdf7e8" style="background-color:#fdf7e8;border-left:4px solid #b8860b;padding:10px 12px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#17313b;">
    <b style="font-family:'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:#8a6508;">THE ACT-NOW CLOCK</b><br>
    <b>Within 48 hours &#8212;</b> Perseid meteor shower peaks the night of <b>Wed Aug 12 into Thu Aug 13</b>; it is a two-night window and then it's gone for a year. Free.<br>
    <b>This week &#8212;</b> the <b>Stern Grove finale (Aug 15&#8211;16)</b> is the last free-lottery weekend of the season; every other 2026 date is already marked sold out. Reserved tables are the only guaranteed seat left &#8212; check the site today.<br>
    <b>Thursday &#8212;</b> <b>49ers preseason home opener</b> vs. Tennessee, Aug 13. Preseason is the one time of year Levi's is genuinely affordable.<br>
    <b>By Aug 21 &#8212;</b> RSVP for <b>Sundown Cinema</b> at Marina Green if you want a shot at reserved seating; the screening itself is free and walk-up.<br>
    <b>Mark the calendar &#8212;</b> <b>Tue Aug 25</b> is a fee-free day across the National Park Service: Muir Woods, Point Reyes and Yosemite all waive admission. Muir Woods still requires a parking/shuttle reservation.
  </td></tr></table>
