<!-- PICK OF THE MONTH -->
<tr><td bgcolor="#fffdf9" style="background-color:#fffdf9;padding:18px 30px 0 30px;">
  <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#fdf7e8" style="background-color:#fdf7e8;border-top:3px solid #b8860b;border-bottom:3px solid #b8860b;">
    <tr><td bgcolor="#fdf7e8" style="background-color:#fdf7e8;padding:14px 16px;">
      <div style="font-family:'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:2px;color:#8a6508;font-weight:bold;">&#9733; PICK OF THE MONTH</div>
      <div style="font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:21px;font-weight:bold;color:#17313b;margin:6px 0 0 0;">Stern Grove Festival, closing weekend: Public Enemy &amp; Al Green</div>
      <div style="font-family:'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;color:#8a6508;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:1px;margin:4px 0 8px 0;">SAT AUG 15 &amp; SUN AUG 16 &middot; SIGMUND STERN GROVE, 19TH AVE &amp; SLOAT, SUNSET &middot; <span style="color:#7a3ea8;">FREE</span> (GA LOTTERY) &middot; ALL AGES</div>
      <p style="font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.65;color:#17313b;margin:0 0 8px 0;">
        <b>Why this one:</b> because it is the last of it. Stern Grove is in its 89th year and this is the final weekend of the 2026 season &#8212; the other eight concerts, June 14 through August 9, are all marked sold out, so Aug 15 and 16 are the only remaining chances to see a free show in the eucalyptus amphitheater this year. The billing is also unusually good even by Grove standards: <b>Saturday</b> is <b>Public Enemy</b> with Vallejo's <b>LaRussell</b> and KPFA's <b>Davey D</b> &#8212; a genuinely Bay-rooted hip-hop bill, not a touring package dropped into a park. <b>Sunday</b> is <b>Al Green</b>, 80 years old, with <b>Goapele</b>, <b>The Glide Ensemble</b> and KALW's Wonway Posibul opening. Two American institutions, one meadow, no ticket price.
      </p>
      <p style="font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#17313b;margin:0 0 8px 0;">
        <b>How to actually get in:</b> general admission is free but distributed by lottery, with reserved tables sold separately and a community box office and partner giveaways alongside. Entry windows open roughly six weeks ahead and close about a week later, so the finale lotteries have likely already run &#8212; check the ticket page today for waitlist or day-of release, and buy a table if you want certainty. <b>Getting there:</b> parking around 19th &amp; Sloat is a known disaster; take Muni (K/M to St. Francis Circle, or the 23/28 buses) and walk in. Gates open well before the music, and the lawn fills early &#8212; arriving two hours out is normal, not paranoid.
      </p>
      <div style="font-family:'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;">
        <a href="https://www.sterngrove.org/lineup2026" style="color:#1f5fbf;font-weight:bold;">2026 lineup &amp; concert pages &#8594;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <a href="https://www.sterngrove.org/ticket-info" style="color:#1f5fbf;font-weight:bold;">Lottery, tables &amp; box office &#8594;</a>
        <span style="color:#5d6d76;font-style:italic;">&nbsp; good for: a blanket, a thermos, and the last warm-ish Sunday of the season</span>
      </div>
    </td></tr>
